PART 1. OFFICIAL ENGLISH LICENSE AGREEMENT
==============================================================================

1. DEFINITIONS
- "Author" refers to the original copyright holder and creator of the Software (smin987).
- "Software" refers collectively to zipper9, including all Source Code,
  documentation, assets, scripts, and Compiled Binaries.
- "Source Code" refers to the human-readable programming language instructions,
  Python scripts, Rust crates, build specs, and assets making up the Software.
- "Compiled Binaries" refers to the machine-executable files, packages, and
  installers (including Windows .exe/.msix, Linux .deb/AppImage/Flatpak, and macOS .dmg/.app)
  officially compiled and published by the Author.
- "Individual" refers to a natural person acting solely on their own personal, non-commercial behalf,
  not on behalf of or for the commercial benefit of any commercial, corporate, or for-profit entity.
- "Corporate Entity & Commercial User" refers to any corporation, company, partnership,
  enterprise, commercial organization, or for-profit entity, as well as any individual
  acting on behalf of, employed by, or utilizing the Software for the commercial operations of such an entity.
- "Competing Product" refers to any software, application, utility, library, tool,
  or service that provides archive compression, decompression, extraction, or
  archival management functionality and is made available or distributed to third parties.
- "Commercial Distribution" refers to any distribution, sale, sublicensing, leasing,
  charging of access/download fees, or commercial bundling with paid products or services.

2. SOURCE CODE TERMS & RESTRICTIONS
The Author makes the Source Code publicly available subject to the following terms:

(a) INDIVIDUAL RESEARCH & CONTRIBUTION GRANT:
    Subject to the terms herein, an Individual is granted a non-exclusive,
    worldwide, royalty-free license to:
    1. Inspect, audit, and review the Source Code for educational learning,
       security transparency, and non-commercial research.
    2. Modify and adapt the Source Code locally and privately on their own
       personal machine solely for internal experimentation and bug analysis.
    3. Fork the official repository solely for the purpose of submitting bug fixes,
       features, or Pull Requests (PRs) back to the official upstream repository
       (https://github.com/smin987/zipper9). All submitted contributions are subject to
       the Contributor License Agreement (CLA) in CONTRIBUTING.md, granting the Author
       irrevocable rights to include contributions in current open-source and future
       commercial, dual-licensed, or proprietary editions.

(b) STRICT PROHIBITION ON MODIFICATION BY COMMERCIAL & CORPORATE USERS:
    Commercial entities, corporations, companies, for-profit organizations/associations,
    and any users acting on their behalf (collectively, "Corporate Entity & Commercial User")
    are strictly PROHIBITED from modifying, altering, patching, or adapting the Source Code,
    whether for internal corporate/business use, evaluation, or external deployment.
    Commercial entities and enterprise users may only execute and deploy the unmodified,
    official Compiled Binaries.

(c) STRICT PROHIBITION ON COMPETING SOFTWARE:
    Neither Individuals nor Corporate Entities & Commercial Users may use the Source Code, in whole
    or in part, modified or unmodified, directly or indirectly, to create,
    develop, market, distribute, release, or license any Competing Product or
    archival service, whether offered for free or for commercial gain.

(d) PROHIBITION ON PUBLIC DISTRIBUTION OF FORKS:
    Public distribution, publishing, hosting, mirroring, or transferring of
    modified Source Code or third-party derivative builds is prohibited without
    the express prior written consent of the Author.

(e) PROHIBITION ON RESALE:
    You may NOT sublicense, rent, lease, sell, or monetize the Source Code.

3. COMPILED BINARIES TERMS: FREE USE GRANT & REDISTRIBUTION
(a) PERPETUAL FREE USE GRANT (INCLUDING COMMERCIAL USE):
    The Author grants all users—including Individuals, educational institutions,
